# src/apps/daemon/internal/networking/routing

## Purpose
Domain, per-app, and rule-based routing policy/data ownership, including embedded domain lists and dynamic override matching.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `networking` (rank 2; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (40): `adaptive_outbound_coordinator.go`, `adaptive_outbound_coordinator_test.go`, `async_rule_evaluator.go`, `async_rule_evaluator_test.go`, `autonomous_routing.go`, `autonomous_routing_test.go`, `autoproxy_matcher.go`, `autoproxy_matcher_test.go`, `canonical_blacklist.go`, `canonical_blacklist_test.go`, `composite_rule_compiler.go`, `composite_rule_compiler_test.go` …
- Child folders: `domain_data/`.

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `routing`.
- Notable exported surface: `AdaptiveOutboundResilienceCoordinator`, `AsyncRuleEvaluator`, `AutoProxyMatcher`, `AutoProxyRuleItem`, `AutoProxyVerdict`, `AutonomousCoordinator`, `CanonicalBlacklistEngine`, `CarrierRoute`, `CarrierType`, `CidrRule` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/networking/diagnostics`, `internal/networking/transport`, `internal/platform/security`.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/networking/proxyconfig`.

## Invariants
- `networking` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

